      "writtenOn": "2023-10-27T20:11:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "LGTM.\n\nThis does have me wondering how much of this logic we should lift out of the colorstop xformer, and just calculate a lot of this when the gradient is constructed?\n\nRight now the xformer is able to go all the way to the dst color space when we don\u0027t have to worry about interpolation spaces, but it seems like it\u0027d be pretty convenient to say that all the colors and stops are calculated and queryable by random access. Then onAppendStages, asFP, or add_to_key for graphite can just convert the colors to the dst space and that\u0027s it. WDYT?",
      "revId": "e25f198dca3041511a0293de4d675f309f949202",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9288154f_cd303905",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 5631
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-10-27T20:21:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That\u0027s a good point. I had continued down the road of adding things to the xformer, because it was already doing the work of going to dest. But at this point, much of this work is independent of the destination color space, so we could hoist it. I\u0027ll probably look at that as a follow-up. (While doing this, I also wondered about getting rid of implicit positions entirely, but we do have CPU code that uses that as a simple signal for fast-path RP stages. We\u0027d probably want a bool to remember that the positions were uniformly spaced).",
      "parentUuid": "3c31f7e9_487eda80",
      "revId": "e25f198dca3041511a0293de4d675f309f949202",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
